    "content": "A fun solution for this that doesn't use strings:\n\nimport math\n\ndef reverse_two_powers(n: int, l: int, u: int) -> int:\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n >= u:\n        return l + reverse_two_powers(n - u, l * 2, u // 2)\n\n    return reverse_two_powers(n, l * 2, u // 2)\n\nn = int(input())\ntwo_power = 2 ** math.floor(math.log2(n))\n\nprint(reverse_two_powers(n, 1, two_power))",
